=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  The web SuspenseProgressBoundary wraps <Suspense> so that while the lazy fallback is
  mounted the global progress bar (lib/globalProgress.ts → TopProgress.tsx) is active, and
  when the children resolve the fallback unmounts and the bar deactivates. SwiftUI has no
  Suspense primitive, so the "is the wrapped content resolving?" signal is bound through a
  P1/S8 state-holder seam (native idiom) instead of a thrown promise; everything else is a
  faithful port.

  - Coordinator (lib/globalProgress.ts): SuspenseProgress is the refcounted @Observable port.
    Constants reproduced verbatim — TRICKLE_TARGET=80, TRICKLE_INITIAL=8, TRICKLE_INTERVAL=120.
    next(p) = p>=80 ? 80 : min(80, p + max(1, (80-p)*0.15)) — 15% of the remaining gap, floor 1,
    clamped. start() returns an idempotent stop; concurrent starts stack; the last stop snaps
    progress to 0 and deactivates. valueNow = round(clamp(p,0,100)) (TopProgress aria-valuenow).
  - Loading host (ProgressTrackingFallback): SuspenseProgressLoadingHost renders the caller's
    fallback and, for exactly as long as it is on screen, holds one coordinator consumer —
    start on appear, stop on disappear — the precise mirror of useEffect(()=>start(),[]).
  - Bar (TopProgress.tsx): SuspenseProgressBar observes the coordinator and paints a 2 pt
    full-width strip; width = trickle %, cyan→indigo→emerald sweep, collapses when inactive,
    width transition omitted under Reduce Motion, role=progressbar with localized label + value.
  - Composition (web fallback/children slots): the boundary is generic over Fallback/Content
    view builders, a drop-in wrapper exactly like the web component. A live boundary is a
    transparent pass-through of its current slot (web parity).
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + a unit test):
      loading (fallback chrome + active global trickle — the web Suspense branch) ·
      content (children rendered transparently — the web children branch) ·
      empty  (resolved with no rows → friendly message, never a blank box — P4 leaf) ·
      error  (async load failed → retry — P4 leaf; web pairs Suspense with an ErrorBoundary) ·
      stale / offline (orthogonal connection axis → banner + inline refresh + one-shot
              auto-refresh on the stale transition — P4 leaf, matches the AiUsageCard precedent).
  - i18n (P1/S10): the one web string — TopProgress aria-label t('global.loading','Loading') —
    is preserved verbatim as suspenseProgress.loadingA11y; the P4 leaf chrome keys
    (empty/errorTitle/retry/staleBanner/offlineBanner/refresh) are namespaced suspenseProgress.*.
    Every code-referenced key is declared in the .strings catalog; NO English string literals in
    native code (all via SuspenseProgressStrings facade + Text(verbatim:)). referenced==declared.
  - Accessibility: the bar exposes a localized label + "{percent}%" value and hides when idle;
    the loading host carries a "Loading" label; the retry button + refresh button carry labels;
    the banner + empty + error compose their children for VoiceOver; Reduce Motion respected.
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened with slug "SuspenseProgressBoundary" emitted exactly once on
    the first presented snapshot (asserted by SpySuspenseProgressTelemetry).

